# Ginga Sengoku Gunyuuden Rai: 16-bit little-endian codes = font cell (12x12 font at file 0x0A8000, 24 B/glyph).
# Keys are the bytes as stored (code 0x039E -> 9E03). Kanji read by eye from tools/font_sheet.py sheets;
# a second copy of a glyph gets a "#2" note only if the font really holds it twice (see docs/re/text.md).
FFFF={end}
# FFFE / FFFD in plain strings: the $81:E962 renderer inserts a name from $00:90DC[$0950] (officer) or
# $00:9C36[$0950] (planet); the $81:E4E5 renderer (vertical names, ship names) treats FFFE as "skip one cell".
# Named by code because the meaning depends on the renderer (docs/re/text.md).
FEFF={FFFE}
FDFF={FFFD}
